{#-
  Maple — deposit / requestRedeem / redeem on ERC-4626-style Maple pools.

  Each entry in deposit_assets pairs a token alias key (the pool's
  UNDERLYING asset) with the pool_alias key used to resolve the pool
  itself. The template resolves the pool via aliases.maple[<pool_alias>]
  with NO existence guard. If the alias is missing on the active chain,
  rendering throws — there is no silent fall-through. To grant the Safe
  access to a pool, add an entry to deposit_assets AND make sure the
  matching pool alias exists in aliases/<chain>/maple.yaml.

  Required template params:
    deposit_assets — list of {asset, pool_alias} entries. Example:
                     [{asset: "USDC", pool_alias: "usdc_pool"}].
                     - aliases.tokens[<asset>]        must exist
                     - aliases.maple[<pool_alias>]    must exist
                     Either lookup missing ⇒ render-time error.

  Exit flow (two-step, Maple-specific):
    Maple pools settle redemptions periodically, so withdrawing is a
    request-then-claim flow:
      1. requestRedeem(shares, owner=safe)       — queues the redemption
      2. (wait for the pool's next settlement)
      3. redeem(shares, receiver=safe, owner=safe) — claims the assets

  Output shape:
    - One approve role per UNIQUE asset; spender = oneOf(every pool whose
      underlying is that asset), so the Safe can approve any in-scope pool
      sharing that underlying to pull it. Multiple pools sharing an
      underlying are aggregated into a single approve role — required, as
      the emit-phase merger rejects duplicate (address, signature) pairs
      within a role key.
    - One deposit / requestRedeem / redeem role per resolved pool, with
      every address parameter pinned to the avatar so shares and assets
      can never be routed off the Safe.
-#}
{%- from "_macros/common.tmpl" import approve -%}
{%- set assets = [] -%}
{%- for entry in deposit_assets -%}
  {%- if entry.asset not in assets -%}
    {%- set _ = assets.push(entry.asset) -%}
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endfor -%}
roles:
{%- for asset in assets %}
  {%- set spenders = [] -%}
  {%- for entry in deposit_assets -%}
    {%- if entry.asset == asset -%}
      {%- set _ = spenders.push(aliases.maple[entry.pool_alias]) -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endfor %}
  {{ approve(aliases.tokens[asset], spenders) | indent(2) }}
{%- endfor %}
{%- for entry in deposit_assets %}
{%- set pool = aliases.maple[entry.pool_alias] %}

  - address: "{{ pool }}"
    functions:
      - signature: "function deposit(uint256 assets, address receiver)"
        execution_options: "none"
        params:
          - name: assets
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "pass"
          - name: receiver
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "equal_to_avatar"

      - signature: "function requestRedeem(uint256 shares, address owner)"
        execution_options: "none"
        params:
          - name: shares
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "pass"
          - name: owner
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "equal_to_avatar"

      - signature: "function redeem(uint256 shares, address receiver, address owner)"
        execution_options: "none"
        params:
          - name: shares
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "pass"
          - name: receiver
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "equal_to_avatar"
          - name: owner
            param_type: "static"
            operator: "equal_to_avatar"
{%- endfor %}
